Caller identity|aws sts get-caller-identity|Returns the account and principal used by the CLI credentials.|Confirm the target identity before diagnosing access or running changes.|Account is the account ID; Arn identifies the user or assumed-role session.|{"Account":"123456789012","Arn":"arn:aws:sts::...:assumed-role/..."}|Read-only API call; select the intended profile and region explicitly where required.
Configured region|aws configure get region|Reads the region configured in the selected profile.|Detect an unexpected profile configuration before regional API calls.|An empty result means this profile setting is absent; environment or command-line configuration can still override region selection.|eu-west-1|Local read; inspect effective environment and explicit --region as well.
Instance inventory|aws ec2 describe-instances --instance-ids INSTANCE_ID|Retrieves configuration and state for selected EC2 instances.|Check AZ, subnet, addresses and lifecycle state.|Reservations contains Instances; State.Name is lifecycle state, not application health.|"State": {"Name":"running"}|Read-only; replace INSTANCE_ID and use the intended account/region.
Security-group rules|aws ec2 describe-security-groups --group-ids GROUP_ID|Returns inbound and outbound rules for a security group.|Check allowed sources, destinations, protocols and ports.|IpPermissions is ingress; IpPermissionsEgress is egress. Group references are different from CIDR ranges.|"FromPort":443,"ToPort":443|Read-only; verify attachment and routing separately.
Route tables|aws ec2 describe-route-tables --filters Name=association.subnet-id,Values=SUBNET_ID|Finds route tables explicitly associated with a subnet.|Inspect next-hop targets for workload traffic.|Routes show destination prefixes and targets; an empty result may mean the subnet uses the VPC main route table.|"DestinationCidrBlock":"0.0.0.0/0"|Read-only; follow up on the VPC main association if no explicit association is returned.
Volume state|aws ec2 describe-volumes --volume-ids VOLUME_ID|Retrieves EBS volume configuration and attachments.|Check AZ compatibility and attachment before host-level storage diagnosis.|State describes volume lifecycle; Attachments identifies instance and device mapping.|"State":"in-use","AvailabilityZone":"..."|Read-only; attached does not mean mounted or application-consistent.
Target health|aws elbv2 describe-target-health --target-group-arn TARGET_GROUP_ARN|Reports load-balancer target health and reason codes.|Diagnose requests failing through a target group.|TargetHealth.State and Reason distinguish initial, unhealthy, draining and other states.|"State":"unhealthy","Reason":"Target.ResponseCodeMismatch"|Read-only; inspect check path, port and expected status alongside the reason.
Scaling groups|aws autoscaling describe-auto-scaling-groups --auto-scaling-group-names GROUP_NAME|Returns group capacity settings and instance membership.|Check desired versus actual capacity during scaling problems.|Compare MinSize, MaxSize, DesiredCapacity and instance lifecycle/health fields.|"DesiredCapacity":3,"Instances":[...]|Read-only; quotas and launch activity may explain a shortfall.
Alarm state|aws cloudwatch describe-alarms --alarm-names ALARM_NAME|Returns alarm definition, state and reason.|Understand what threshold, period and missing-data policy produced a page.|StateValue is OK, ALARM or INSUFFICIENT_DATA; StateReason explains recent evaluation.|"StateValue":"ALARM"|Read-only; use the correct region and inspect the underlying metric population.
Recent account events|aws cloudtrail lookup-events --max-results 10|Retrieves recent matching management-event history.|Find configuration changes near an incident.|EventName, Username and EventTime identify actions; inspect the embedded event for resource and error details.|"EventName":"Modify...","EventTime":"..."|Read-only; event history coverage is limited and does not include every data event.
Queue attributes|aws sqs get-queue-attributes --queue-url QUEUE_URL --attribute-names All|Reads queue configuration and approximate message counts.|Check visibility timeout, retention and backlog indicators.|ApproximateNumberOfMessages is visible backlog; NotVisible represents in-flight messages, not completed work.|"VisibilityTimeout":"30"|Read-only; approximate counts are not an exact transactional inventory.
Bucket versioning|aws s3api get-bucket-versioning --bucket BUCKET|Reads the bucket's versioning configuration.|Check whether earlier object versions may exist for recovery.|Status Enabled or Suspended describes versioning configuration; an absent status differs from enabled.|{"Status":"Enabled"}|Read-only; verify actual object versions and lifecycle retention before promising recovery.
Configuration source|aws configure list|Displays resolved CLI configuration values and their sources.|Find an unexpected profile, region or credential source before calling other APIs.|Type and Location explain where each value came from; keys are masked but account identity still needs STS verification.|Name Value Type Location|Read-only; do not share even masked credential diagnostics unnecessarily.
Available profiles|aws configure list-profiles|Lists named profiles in local AWS configuration.|Choose the intended configuration context for a task.|Each line is a profile name, not proof of current authentication or account identity.|staging / production|Read-only local inspection. Use --profile explicitly on subsequent commands when needed.
SSO session login|aws sso login --profile PROFILE|Starts the configured IAM Identity Center authentication flow.|Obtain a normal CLI session for an authorized profile.|Follow the displayed device/browser flow; successful login caches session material locally but does not validate every service permission.|Successfully logged into Start URL...|Authentication action; use your own authorized account and configured profile. Never paste tokens into shared logs.
Instance status checks|aws ec2 describe-instance-status --instance-ids INSTANCE_ID --include-all-instances|Retrieves EC2 system and instance status checks.|Separate host/platform health from guest operating-system health.|SystemStatus and InstanceStatus have separate checks; passed checks do not prove the application works.|"SystemStatus":{"Status":"ok"}|Read-only API call; set intended account/Region and ensure EC2 describe permissions.
Network interface detail|aws ec2 describe-network-interfaces --network-interface-ids ENI_ID|Retrieves interface addresses, attachments and associated groups.|Trace the actual network attachment of an affected workload.|PrivateIpAddresses, SubnetId, Groups and Attachment identify addressing and placement.|"SubnetId":"subnet-...","Status":"in-use"|Read-only; output contains internal addressing. Verify Region and interface identity.
Subnet ACL rules|aws ec2 describe-network-acls --filters Name=association.subnet-id,Values=SUBNET_ID|Lists network ACLs associated with a subnet.|Check stateless filtering on both request and return paths.|Entries include RuleNumber, Egress, action and port range; lower matching rule numbers take precedence.|"RuleAction":"allow","Egress":false|Read-only; evaluate ephemeral return ports and both directions with the actual traffic flow.
NAT gateway state|aws ec2 describe-nat-gateways --nat-gateway-ids NAT_ID|Retrieves NAT gateway state, subnet and addressing.|Check whether a planned outbound translation path exists and is available.|State describes the gateway lifecycle; available does not prove route tables or destination access are correct.|"State":"available"|Read-only; correlate with routing, metrics and the originating subnet.
VPC endpoint policy|aws ec2 describe-vpc-endpoints --vpc-endpoint-ids ENDPOINT_ID|Retrieves endpoint configuration, associations and policy.|Investigate private access to an AWS service.|ServiceName and VpcEndpointType identify the service/path; route tables or network interfaces depend on endpoint type.|"VpcEndpointType":"Gateway","State":"available"|Read-only; endpoint policy is only one part of authorization.
Object metadata|aws s3api head-object --bucket BUCKET --key KEY|Retrieves metadata for one object without downloading its body.|Check object size, version information and encryption metadata.|ContentLength is bytes; ETag is not universally a plain MD5 checksum, especially for multipart or encrypted uploads.|"ContentLength":4096,"ServerSideEncryption":"aws:kms"|Read-only; requires relevant access. Denial does not establish whether the object exists.
Retained object versions|aws s3api list-object-versions --bucket BUCKET --prefix KEY|Lists retained versions and delete markers matching a prefix.|Identify a recovery candidate after accidental overwrite or deletion.|VersionId, IsLatest and LastModified distinguish versions; prefix can match more than one exact object key.|"Versions":[{"Key":"config.json","VersionId":"..."}]|Read-only; inspect the exact key and retained version before any restoration.
Bucket public-access guardrails|aws s3api get-public-access-block --bucket BUCKET|Retrieves bucket-level Block Public Access settings.|Review guardrails during an exposure investigation.|Four booleans describe controls on public ACLs and policies; account-level controls and access policies also matter.|"BlockPublicPolicy":true|Read-only; this output alone is not a complete effective-access audit.
Bucket encryption defaults|aws s3api get-bucket-encryption --bucket BUCKET|Reads the bucket's default server-side encryption configuration.|Check the encryption policy applied to new uploads by default.|SSEAlgorithm identifies the configured mechanism; KMS settings may name a key.|"SSEAlgorithm":"aws:kms"|Read-only; defaults do not retroactively prove the encryption state of every existing object.
Database instance configuration|aws rds describe-db-instances --db-instance-identifier DB_ID|Retrieves RDS instance state and configuration.|Inspect availability, endpoint and backup settings during diagnosis.|DBInstanceStatus is lifecycle state; Endpoint, MultiAZ and BackupRetentionPeriod describe separate properties.|"DBInstanceStatus":"available","MultiAZ":true|Read-only; available does not prove client connectivity or query correctness.
Lambda configuration|aws lambda get-function-configuration --function-name FUNCTION_NAME|Reads a function's runtime, limits and execution configuration.|Investigate timeout, memory or deployment configuration changes.|Timeout is seconds; MemorySize is MB; LastUpdateStatus reports configuration update progress.|"Timeout":30,"MemorySize":512|Read-only but output may contain environment variables. Protect secrets and verify function version/alias context.
DynamoDB table state|aws dynamodb describe-table --table-name TABLE_NAME|Retrieves table metadata, key schema and capacity-mode information.|Check the intended schema and resource state during throttling investigation.|TableStatus describes lifecycle; KeySchema names partition/sort keys. ItemCount is an approximate periodically updated value.|"TableStatus":"ACTIVE"|Read-only; inspect metrics for actual hot-key or throughput behavior.
Encryption key metadata|aws kms describe-key --key-id KEY_ID|Retrieves KMS key metadata without performing decryption.|Check key state, origin and intended usage.|KeyState can be Enabled, Disabled or another lifecycle state; KeyUsage identifies permitted operation class.|"KeyState":"Enabled","KeyUsage":"ENCRYPT_DECRYPT"|Read-only; an enabled key can still deny a caller through policy or conditions.
Secret rotation metadata|aws secretsmanager describe-secret --secret-id SECRET_ID|Retrieves secret metadata without the secret value.|Check rotation settings and version staging during credential incidents.|RotationEnabled and VersionIdsToStages show configuration and version labels, not whether every consumer refreshed.|"RotationEnabled":true|Read-only metadata; do not use get-secret-value merely to diagnose staging information.
DNS record inventory|aws route53 list-resource-record-sets --hosted-zone-id ZONE_ID|Lists DNS record sets in a hosted zone.|Check configured routing records before comparing resolver answers.|Name, Type and TTL identify records; alias targets use different fields and do not expose a normal record TTL here.|"Name":"api.example.com.","Type":"A"|Read-only; the hosted zone may be public or private. Configuration is not proof all caches updated.
